WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.500
The morning sun rises over the hills of Bugesera.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Below the horizon, cranes, runways, and terminal structures
are becoming a new gateway to Rwanda.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
This is Bugesera International Airport,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:26.000
a modern aviation hub designed to welcome travellers,
connect businesses, and carry Rwandan stories into the world.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.000
For years, Kigali International Airport has served
as Rwanda’s doorway to the globe.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.000
But as passenger numbers grow and national ambitions rise,

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.000
a larger, more efficient facility is needed.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Bugesera is planned to handle bigger aircraft,
increasing traffic, and future expansion,

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.000
improving the journey from arrival to departure.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.000
When completed, the terminal presents
a calm, contemporary face:

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:02.000
broad drop-off zones, clean lines, glass façades,
and clear multilingual signage.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Inside, daylight fills the check-in hall,
making the space feel open and accessible.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Wide walkways, tactile guidance paths, and audible announcements
help every passenger move with confidence.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.000
A departing traveller steps from a taxi
into a hall designed for clarity.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Self-service kiosks offer speed, while staffed counters
support families and those needing assistance.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.000
After check-in, luggage moves along conveyors
into sorting systems.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Passengers continue through security screening,
then immigration,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.000
where separate lanes manage residents, visitors,
transit passengers, and crew.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Beyond formalities, the terminal opens into lounges
with shops, cafés, charging points, and quiet seating.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:07.000
Arrivals follow an equally guided path.
After the aircraft parks, passengers move

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.000
through the jet bridge into the terminal.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.000
International travellers first reach immigration,
verifying passports and entry documents.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:23.000
Then they proceed to baggage reclaim, where large carousels
and real time-flight displays,  make it easier to idenify the correct belt.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.000
After collecting luggage, passengers pass
through customs and enter through the arrivals halls,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:34.000
where taxis, shuttles, ride-hailing bays,
and public transport links await.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.000
Outside, the runway gives the airport its rhythm.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:43.000
An aircraft approaches through the East African sky,
guided by air traffic controls into final alignment.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.000
Landing gear lowers, flaps extend,
and the plane touches down smoothly on the center line.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:55.000
Spoilers and thrust reversers slow it,
while runway marking and edge lights keep the path clear.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:05.000
The aircraft exits to a taxiway, moving toward its assigned stand,
where ground crews fuel trucks, catering vans, baggae crew prepare it for the next journey.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.000
But Bugesera is more than passenger halls and runways.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Cargo facilities allow Rwandan products—
coffee, tea, flowers, pharmaceuticals,
and manufactured goods—

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.000
to reach international markets quickly.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:26.000
Fuel farms, maintenance areas, fire stations, and control towers operate behind the scenes, keeping the airport safe, secure, and reliable.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:35.000
Connected by roads and future transport links to Kigali and the wider region, Bugesera is built to support tourism, trade, and regional integration.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:42.000
When the terminal glows at dusk and planes continue to land, Rwanda’s new gateway sends a clear message:

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.000
the country is ready to meet the world.

